== Effects ==
* Upon use, spawns a random item from the current room's [[Item Pool|item pool]], with a base ~17% chance to spawn {{i|A Lump of Coal}} or {{i|The Poop}} instead.

== Notes ==
* The chance to get {{i|A Lump of Coal}} or {{i|The Poop}} is determined by [[Luck]] using this formula: <math>\frac2 { 12 + \left \lfloor \mathit{Luck}  \right \rfloor}</math>
** A table showing an example is below. There's no cap, with diminishing returns. At 88 Luck the chance drops to 2%.
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Luck !! Item Pool !! Poop/Coal
|-
| -10 || 0% || 100%
|-
| 0 || 83.3% || 16.6%
|-
| 8 || 90%|| 10%
|}
* A Lump of Coal and The Poop are fixed drops, and cannot be changed by having {{i|Chaos}}, holding {{t|NO!|n}}, and other similar effects. This also means Mystery Gift can drop copies of either item even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed them.
* Spawning The Poop will create a [[Status Effects#Poison|poison]] cloud, as if having used {{I|The Bean}}, down to matching the former item's effects.

== Synergies ==
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns a random wisp. For the rest of the run, a random wisp spawns after clearing a room if the one given by the item was destroyed, including the replacement wisps given by this effect.}}
* {{i|Damocles}}: When Damocles is activated, a second item will be spawned with adherence to the item pool for the current room. Even if Mystery Gift "fails" and spawns either {{i|The Poop}} or {{i|A Lump of Coal}}, a second item from the current room's item pool will always be rewarded.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Car Battery|n}}: No effect, Mystery Gift will only spawn a single item.
* {{i|Void|n}}: Like all single-use active items, this item cannot be absorbed by Void. Instead, it will consume and use the Mystery Gift.
** {{dlc|r}} Mystery Gift will be absorbed and will spawn the item upon Void's next use.

